# Format and Clippy before handoff

After editing Rust code in this workspace, before telling the user the work is done:

1. Run `cargo fmt` on the crates you changed (or the workspace).
2. Run `cargo clippy` on those crates (`--all-targets` when practical).
3. Fix new issues you introduced. Do not “fix” by silencing lints unless the project already does so for that case.
4. Do not change git submodules (`protobuf-core`, `unmanaged`) to satisfy workspace-only lint policy unless the user explicitly asks.

If fmt/clippy fails because of a pre-existing submodule or unrelated problem, report it; do not workaround by editing those crates unprompted.
